    "answer": "YES - condition 5's re-merge trigger fired (it had NOT fired at review time; the verdict recorded two commits, neither touching packages/spec).",
    "commands": "git fetch origin main; git log --oneline 5023630b1788c497355ea6fa4194c444e35d578f..origin/main -- packages/spec  and  git diff --name-only 5023630b1788c497355ea6fa4194c444e35d578f origin/main -- packages/spec",
    "finding": "origin/main moved 5023630b1 -> ed9d87653, six commits. Exactly one touches packages/spec: 615fac3a0 'fix(lint,metadata-protocol): a Studio publish refuses an object whose highlightFields ... names a missing field', and it touches exactly one file there, packages/spec/src/api/protocol.test.ts.",
    "action_taken": "Ran bash scripts/pm/os-regen-merge.sh in the worktree (exit 0). Step 1 merged origin/main by ort, 26 files, no conflicts. Step 2 KEPT the branch's bytes of all five os-regen paths it examined (the three reference mdx files plus authorable-surface/system.json and authorable-defaults/system.json) because the branch changed them and main did not - the script's measured anti-revert case. Step 3 reported the merge left no additional changes to commit. Step 4 (mine): rebuilt and ran check:generated - 'All 15 generated artifacts are up to date' with a clean tree afterwards, so regeneration was a no-op and there is NO separate regeneration commit; nothing to commit is the honest outcome, not a skipped step. Sibling-swallow assertion: git diff origin/main HEAD -- packages/spec/src/migrations/registry.ts shows exactly ONE removed line, and it is the branch's own string-literal continuation being extended ('it never had an effect to lose).' becoming that text plus ' + ' and the new deadline-keys sentences) - no sibling entry and no previous implementation body was dropped. All three semantic ids and the three nested registrations are still present at HEAD.",
    "merge_base_note": "The repo is a shallow checkout and 'git merge-base HEAD origin/main' answered 5023630b1, which looked wrong at first because HEAD is a merge of origin/main. Resolved structurally rather than by trusting the shallow walk: git rev-list --parents -n 1 HEAD shows HEAD's two parents are 4ad24c0b6 (the work commit) and 5023630b1 itself, so 5023630b1 is the true merge base and matches the base the reviewer used. The PR JSON's base.sha 20032594f is the base BRANCH TIP, not a merge base - it is an ancestor of origin/main (is-ancestor exit 0, self-certifying) but not of the pre-merge HEAD."
  },
